## Audit Types

### 1. JWT & Auth Review

**Trigger:** Any change to auth endpoints, token generation, middleware, token storage, password hashing, or RBAC logic.

**Checks:**
- JWT signed with strong secret (HS256 minimum, RS256 preferred for scale)
- `exp` claim present and reasonably short (access: 15-60min, refresh: days)
- JWT secret stored securely (vault, SSM SecureString, or equivalent) -- never in code or committed `.env`
<% if (modules.mobile) { %>
<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind') { %>
- Mobile: tokens stored in `expo-secure-store` or platform keychain -- **never** `AsyncStorage`
<% } else if (mobileFramework === 'flutter') { %>
- Mobile: tokens stored in `flutter_secure_storage` or platform keychain -- **never** `SharedPreferences`
<% } %>
<% } %>
<% if (modules.web) { %>
- Web: tokens in httpOnly cookie or in-memory only -- **never** `localStorage`
<% } %>
- 401 responses never leak whether a user exists (timing-safe comparison)
- Refresh token rotation implemented (invalidate old refresh on use)
- Strong password hashing (Argon2 or bcrypt) -- never change algorithm without migration plan
- RBAC enforced per resource scope, not globally
- Rate limiting on all auth routes: login, register, password reset, token refresh
