### 2. Backend Code Review

**Trigger:** New route, new service with user data, file upload, new dependency.

**Checks organized by OWASP Top 10:**

| OWASP Category | What to Check |
|---|---|
<% if (backendFramework === 'fastapi-sqlalchemy' || backendFramework === 'django') { %>
| **Injection (SQL/NoSQL)** | ORM used, no raw string SQL with f-strings or `.format()`. All queries parameterized. |
<% } else { %>
| **Injection (SQL/NoSQL)** | ORM/query builder used, no raw string interpolation in queries. All queries parameterized. |
<% } %>
| **Broken Authentication** | Tokens validated on every request, refresh uses rotation, sessions expire properly. |
| **Sensitive Data Exposure** | No passwords, tokens, or PII in API responses. Serialization schemas exclude sensitive fields. |
| **Broken Access Control / IDOR** | Ownership check before returning or modifying any resource. Endpoints without permission checks flagged. |
| **SSRF** | User inputs never used directly in server-side HTTP requests without validation/allowlisting. |
<% if (backendFramework === 'fastapi-sqlalchemy') { %>
| **Mass Assignment** | Pydantic schemas do not accept non-editable fields (e.g., `is_admin`, `role`, `owner_id`). |
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'django') { %>
| **Mass Assignment** | Serializers do not accept non-editable fields (e.g., `is_admin`, `role`, `owner_id`). |
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'nestjs') { %>
| **Mass Assignment** | DTOs do not accept non-editable fields (e.g., `isAdmin`, `role`, `ownerId`). |
<% } else { %>
| **Mass Assignment** | Input schemas/DTOs do not accept non-editable fields (e.g., `isAdmin`, `role`, `ownerId`). |
<% } %>
| **Rate Limiting** | Sensitive routes (auth, password reset, OTP) have rate limits configured. |
| **Security Misconfiguration** | No hardcoded secrets, debug mode off in production, CORS origins explicit (not `*`). |
| **File Upload** | MIME type validated server-side (not just extension), file size limits enforced, filename sanitized, secure storage destination. |
| **Error Handling** | No stack traces, internal paths, or DB error messages in production responses. |

<% if (backendFramework === 'fastapi-sqlalchemy') { %>
- Input validation via Pydantic -- no raw request body access
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'django') { %>
- Input validation via Serializers -- no raw request body access
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'nestjs') { %>
- Input validation via DTOs with class-validator -- no raw request body access
<% } else { %>
- Input validation via schema/DTO layer -- no raw request body access
<% } %>
- CORS: allowed origins explicit and restrictive
- File uploads: validate MIME type server-side; apply file type whitelist
<% } %>
