## Severity Levels

| Level | Tag | Meaning | Response Time |
|---|---|---|---|
| Critical | `[SECURITY: CRITICAL]` | Block everything, fix before any merge | Immediate -- blocks release |
| High | `[SECURITY: HIGH]` | Fix in this PR before merge | Same PR / same day |
| Medium | `[SECURITY: MEDIUM]` | Fix within the week | Next sprint at latest |
| Low | `[SECURITY: LOW]` | Track and address next cycle | Backlog |

**Examples by severity:**
- **Critical:** Auth bypass, exposed secret in repo, SQL injection, IDOR on sensitive data, compromised credentials
- **High:** Missing ownership check, overpermissioned IAM role, XSS, token in localStorage, missing RBAC
- **Medium:** Missing rate limiting, verbose error messages, dependency with known CVE, permissive CORS
- **Low:** Missing security headers, minor info disclosure, outdated TLS on non-critical endpoint

