## Output Format

### Primary Output: Findings Table

```markdown
## Security Report

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|---|---|
| Critical | 0 |
| High | 0 |
| Medium | 0 |
| Low | 0 |

### Findings

| # | Severity | Category | File | Description | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | CRITICAL | Auth | app/core/config.py:12 | JWT secret hardcoded in code | Move to secure vault/SSM |
| 2 | HIGH | IDOR | app/api/routes/items.py:45 | PUT endpoint without ownership check | Add ownership verification |
| 3 | MEDIUM | Rate Limit | app/api/routes/auth.py:30 | Login route without rate limiting | Apply rate limiter (5 req/min) |
| 4 | LOW | Headers | app/main.py | Strict-Transport-Security header missing | Add security headers middleware |
```

### Secondary Output: Inline Severity Tags

For quick scanning in code review contexts, also produce inline tags:

```
[SECURITY: CRITICAL] JWT secret hardcoded in app/core/config.py line 12 -- move to secure vault
[SECURITY: HIGH] POST /api/v1/items/{id} without ownership check -- any user can modify
[SECURITY: MEDIUM] Login endpoint without rate limiting -- brute force possible
[SECURITY: LOW] CloudFront without Strict-Transport-Security header
```

### Positive Findings Section

Always include a section documenting what is already well implemented:

```markdown
### Positive Findings

- Strong password hashing implemented correctly
- Refresh tokens with rotation active
- Proper access control on critical endpoints
```

### Action Plan

End every report with a prioritized action list:

```markdown
### Prioritized Action Plan

1. [CRITICAL] Move JWT secret to secure vault -- Responsible: **backend**
2. [HIGH] Add ownership check on /items -- Responsible: **backend**
3. [MEDIUM] Implement rate limiting on /auth/login -- Responsible: **backend**
4. [LOW] Add security headers -- Responsible: **backend**
```

